  id: W5_C
  era: "1920s\u20131940s"
  title: A spinning wheel, or charkha (replica)
  text: "A spinning wheel, or charkha (replica). Gandhi urged every Indian to spin cotton every day. Spinning khadi \u2013 hand-spun, hand-woven cloth \u2013 was a way to boycott British mill cloth, give work to villagers and show self-reliance. In 1921 a spinning wheel was placed at the centre of a proposed national flag, the forerunner of the Ashoka Chakra on today's tricolour. Bonfires of foreign cloth were lit across India during the Non-Cooperation Movement, and wearing khadi became a badge of the freedom struggle."
  narration: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8a10b0bb132d349a590e16393ab587c0, type: 3}
